/T (Every time the program asks for something, it checks the answer and asks again if it is not valid. Amounts must be positive numbers \(commas are allowed, so 1,500 works\). Dates must follow YYYY-MM-DD and cannot be in the future. Text fields cannot be empty. Because of this, a typing mistake never crashes the program or saves bad data.)
/E (Every time the program asks for something, it checks the answer and asks again if it is not valid. Amounts must be positive numbers \(commas are allowed, so 1,500 works\). Dates must follow YYYY-MM-DD and cannot be in the future. Text fields cannot be empty. Because of this, a typing mistake never crashes the program or saves bad data.)
